Subject: Jupiter 7 Plus and phone calls to California

          Hi.

          I spoke with the Jupiter people. Apparently, there are 6 handshake
lines in the Jupiter parallel interface -- it really is designed for
DMA, not for "standard" centronix-type parallel I/O. However, Jupiter
makes a board which plugs into the Jupiter and gives it a standard
centronix parallel port. Then we could just plug the cabel form the IBM
into the Jupiter, and the data transfer rate would be much higher. The
catch is that the board costs $1500.

          I explained the the engineer the kind of problems I've been having
and we decided that what might be happening is this: There might be a
byte being lost someplace, and the Jupiter is then interperting the
following command arguments as actual commands, (the problem with inband
control...) It's given me some ideas where to look, but for now, atleast
the setup works from nick.

          Fonts will hopefully be working by Tuesday night.

................................................................simson

